=========================================================================
GOVERNING RULE — LEATHER & KILIM ARE ALWAYS SEPARATE PRODUCTS
=========================================================================
Leather and kilim are NEVER a construction toggle on one product. Each is its
own product / PDP. Both are FIXED PRICE per size, with free line-item property
pickers (no priced finish axis).

  LEATHER product: full Leather Colour picker + Metal Finish.
  KILIM product:  Kilim shown as a FIXED LABEL (with trust note) + a LIMITED
                  Leather Trim picker + Metal Finish.

Wherever kilim is the main top fabric on ANY furniture category, the PDP shows:
one fixed Kilim + leather trim (limited) + metal finish. Leather-only pieces
show the full leather colour range + metal finish.

=========================================================================
ENGINE MAPPING (why the JSON looks like a 'grid')
=========================================================================
Both patterns run on the GRID engine. The CONSTRUCTION axis (Leather | Kilim)
has exactly ONE value per product, so the engine renders it as a static fixed
label (mat_count==1 path) — no toggle. Pickers ride on top via cfg.pickers[].

The SIZE axis may be single OR multiple:
  - Single size  -> one variant, size button hidden, dims shown from the one key.
  - Multiple sizes (e.g. Square / Rectangular) -> one variant PER size, size
    buttons shown, price + dims switch per size automatically.
All variants: inventoryPolicy CONTINUE (made to order).

The leather picker uses branch_by_axis:true so it filters via tier_filters keyed
by the single Construction value. include_names limits which swatches show (kilim).

=========================================================================
*** DIMENSIONS RULE — READ THIS, IT IS THE #1 GOTCHA ***
=========================================================================
The grid engine reads dimensions from the aav.size_dimensions metafield, KEYED
BY THE EXACT SIZE-BUTTON VALUE (case + spelling must match the option value).
cfg.unit_map is the fallback and must carry the SAME keys.
The dim_w / dim_d / dim_h number fields are NOT read by the grid engine.

Whenever you ADD, RENAME, or REMOVE a size value you MUST update BOTH
aav.size_dimensions and cfg.unit_map to have one matching key per size value.
If a size button has no matching key, the dimensions box renders EMPTY.

Example — a product with sizes [Square, Rectangular]:
  aav.size_dimensions =
    {"Square":{"cm":"45 × 45 × 45 cm","in":"17.7 × 17.7 × 17.7 in"},
     "Rectangular":{"cm":"90 × 45 × 45 cm","in":"35.4 × 17.7 × 17.7 in"}}
  cfg.unit_map =
    {"Square":"45 × 45 × 45 cm","Rectangular":"90 × 45 × 45 cm"}
  (cm->in: 45->17.7, 90->35.4, 60->23.6, 120->47.2, 75->29.5)

